### `dice_roller.py` — what it does

| Feature | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Default run** | `python dice_roller.py` → rolls a single d6 |
| **Pick die size** | `--sides 20` for a d20, `--sides 100` for a d%, etc. |
| **Multiple rolls** | `--rolls 4` to roll several dice at once |
| **Visual bar** | Each result shows a `█/░` progress bar so you can eyeball the roll at a glance |
| **Running total** | When rolling multiple dice it prints the sum with the min/max range |

It uses only Python's standard library (`random`, `argparse`), so no packages to install — just run it directly.

